;; 永 (yǒng, "eternity") — the Eight Principles of Yong.
;; Five physical strokes, written in conventional order. The eight principles
;; are distributed across the strokes as brush pressure and direction changes:
;; 側 dot; 勒 horizontal; 努 vertical; 趯 hook; 策 rising entry;
;; 掠 left sweep; 啄 short right entry; 磔 right sweep.
;;
;; Black ink is palette colour 5 (script-only; the interactive UI still shows
;; the original four colour swatches).
paint/draw-clear
paint/set-tool 3
paint/set-color 5
paint/set-calligraphy-diameter 54
paint/set-ink-opacity 255

;; 1. 側 — top dot. Heavy contact, then a tapered descending point.
paint/draw-pressure-line 398 108 190 383 128 175
paint/draw-pressure-line 383 128 175 366 158 10

;; 2. 勒 / 策 — horizontal with a light rising entry, weighted centre and
;; controlled finish at the top of the central vertical.
paint/draw-pressure-line 238 222 55 272 214 160
paint/draw-pressure-line 272 214 160 352 204 230
paint/draw-pressure-line 352 204 230 408 201 165

;; 3. 努 / 趯 — firm vertical, then a compact upward-left hook.
paint/draw-pressure-line 405 200 170 400 290 210
paint/draw-pressure-line 400 290 210 405 405 225
paint/draw-pressure-line 405 405 225 400 432 135
paint/draw-pressure-line 400 432 135 386 440 60
paint/draw-pressure-line 386 440 60 362 418 6

;; 4. 掠 — long left sweep, broadening under pressure and tapering to a point.
paint/draw-pressure-line 400 275 165 356 326 210
paint/draw-pressure-line 356 326 210 292 402 155
paint/draw-pressure-line 292 402 155 220 500 8

;; 5. 啄 / 磔 — one continuous right stroke: short down-left entry (啄),
;; pressure at the turn, then the expanding right sweep (磔) with a sharp exit.
paint/draw-pressure-line 505 240 35 480 272 150
paint/draw-pressure-line 480 272 150 455 300 215
paint/draw-pressure-line 455 300 215 505 360 245
paint/draw-pressure-line 505 360 245 560 425 225
paint/draw-pressure-line 560 425 225 600 490 10
